<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/producers/proof-src-55b91225bf2dba46> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/retainedSource> "% SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Blackcat Informatics® Inc. <paudley@blackcatinformatics.ca>\n% SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0\n%\n% A TSTP derivation produced by OUR OWN reasoner — no external prover was\n% involved. Source problem:\n%   conformance/logic/cases/external/tptp-mini/theorem-subclass/source/problem.p\n%   (a ⊑ b, b ⊑ c ⊢ a ⊑ c; SZS status Theorem)\n%\n% How it was produced:\n%   1. `gmeow_conformance::external::tptp::parse_tptp` parses the problem.\n%   2. `gmeow_conformance::external::tptp::lower_to_fol_program` reduces the\n%      refutation `premises ∧ ¬conjecture` into the Horn fragment: the conjecture\n%      ∀X.(a(X) → c(X)) is negated through the shared `gmeow_logic::entail::negate`\n%      waist, whose fresh reserved-namespace witness w yields the asserted fact\n%      a(w) and the goal c(w).\n%   3. `gmeow_logic::proof_tree::prove_reasoning_program` resolves that goal with\n%      the PurRDF proof-carrying SLG-WFS backward engine\n%      (`purrdf::datalog::resolve_fol`) and VALIDATES every answer's proof term\n%      with PurRDF's Curry–Howard checker\n%      (`purrdf::datalog::resolve_fol::check_fol_proof`), which independently\n%      re-derives each conclusion from its premises.\n%   4. `ProofTree::to_tstp` projects the checked proof term to the lines below.\n%\n% The derivation of c(w) from a(w) IS the refutation: it contradicts the negated\n% conjecture's ¬c(w).\n%\n% Reading the surface:\n%   * Each step name `d_<hex>` is the exact image of that step's content-addressed\n%     derivation IRI, `https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/derivation/<hex>`,\n%     where `<hex>` is PurRDF's `derivation_id` — a SHA-1 over the proof's rule\n%     identity and its recursive sub-proof digests. gmeow derives the IRI from\n%     PurRDF's content digest; PurRDF itself mints no IRIs.\n%   * Predicates, constants, and inference-rule identities are IRIs, so they ride\n%     as TPTP single-quoted atoms rather than being lossily shortened.\n%   * An `inference(...)` rule IRI names the fired clause's content-addressed\n%     identity (`.../gmeow/goal-directed/rule/<blake3>`, a blake3 digest of\n%     PurRDF's `rule_identity`), which is what the proof checker re-derives against.\n%   * Leaves are `axiom` (asserted EDB facts); derived steps are `plain`.\ncnf(d_b17bff2379a308d9d6b50b0f9a073ef5e051b853, axiom, 'https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/tptp#a'('https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/entail/reserved#witness-d4a1e02579180296')).\ncnf(d_0e9d1c683cc59b3da5626f16bd835a646aefd1ac, plain, 'https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/tptp#b'('https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/entail/reserved#witness-d4a1e02579180296'), inference('https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/goal-directed/rule/c4baaa462517cae869dfedd50b8efef4afaf2fe9037b1f0c4f5e520f9200ffdf', [status(thm)], [d_b17bff2379a308d9d6b50b0f9a073ef5e051b853])).\ncnf(d_2f2cb9320e4a9d0302cb5797a1e21f10d26a3e26, plain, 'https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/tptp#c'('https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/entail/reserved#witness-d4a1e02579180296'), inference('https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/goal-directed/rule/772035b62784cf12dce87129ba59bf14365477017a1c8c5fed58ada7d4ad35be', [status(thm)], [d_0e9d1c683cc59b3da5626f16bd835a646aefd1ac])).\n" .
